   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\ngranted to the county of Clinton to impose an additional one percent of sales\nand compensating use taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S4735",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4735-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4735\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\ngranted to the county of Clinton to impose an additional one percent of\nsales and compensating use taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize Clinton County to extend its sales and compensating tax an\nadditional one percent for two additional years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Authorizes Clinton County to extend its sales and compensat-\ning tax through Nov. 30, 2025.\n\nSection 2 - Provides effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn Feb 8, 2023, the Clinton County Legislature approved a resolution\nseeking an extension of its authority to impose an additional one\npercent of sales and compensating tax for three years. The county's\nexisting authority is set to expire on Nov. 30, 2023.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
